# AI Agent Patterns and Guidelines

## Status: Phase 8 Complete ✅

The AI movie recommendation agent uses LangGraph.js for orchestration, AWS Bedrock as the LLM, and integrates with existing TMDB APIs and user data from MongoDB.

### Supported Models

The agent supports multiple Bedrock models via the `BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` env variable:

| Model | ID | Notes |
|-------|-----|-------|
| Amazon Nova Pro | `apac.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0` | **Default, recommended** - proper tool calling |
| Claude 3 Haiku | `us.anthropic.claude-3-haiku-20240307-v1:0` | Fast, cost-effective |

**⚠️ Kimi K2 NOT Recommended:** `moonshot.kimi-k2-thinking` has non-standard tool calling behavior - it outputs tool calls as text tokens instead of structured API calls, which breaks LangChain's tool execution. Use Nova Pro or Claude instead.

**Streaming Support:** Uses SSE format for responses. Tool calls use non-streaming invoke for reliability (ensures tools actually execute).

